{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "label": "PersistentActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "intro", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Event-sourcing base class: commands are validated and decide which facts happened; those events are persisted and then folded into state by a pure handler. On startup the journal is replayed so the actor resumes where the last instance left off."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_initialstate", "label": "initialState()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## The three abstract methods", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The state before any events; the base onEvent builds on top of it, so it is also what a history with a missing beginning would be wrongly folded onto."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "label": "onEvent(state, event)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### `onEvent(state, event)`", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure and synchronous on purpose: the same events replay many times, so a side effect inside it duplicates on every recovery. It is synchronous while onCommand is async because deciding does I/O while folding a fact into state is arithmetic. State must be read from the parameter, never this.state, because replay runs it detached before this.state is assigned (DevTools time-travel borrows it the same way)."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_oncommand", "label": "onCommand(state, command)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### `onCommand(state, command)`", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Validates against current state and decides what to persist. Three valid outcomes: persist, reply without persisting, or reject. Async because persist writes to the journal."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persist", "label": "persist(event, afterPersist)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## The `persist` callback", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Three guarantees make it the transaction boundary for command processing: the event is durable, onEvent has run so state reflects it, and incoming commands are stashed for the duration so nothing interleaves. Side effects belong in the callback because it runs exactly once per event."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceid", "label": "persistenceId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Persistence ID", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Identifies the event stream in the journal; two actors sharing one would share the same event log, which is usually a bug. For per-entity actors it is derived from the entity id."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceidvalidation", "label": "Persistence ID validation rules", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### What a persistence ID may contain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An ID is more than a value: it names a stream and several backends build a structured storage key out of it, so preStart refuses empty IDs, IDs over 255 characters (the relational persistence_id column width and part of its primary key), slashes (object storage lays an ID out as a directory), '.'/'..' (traversal), and control characters (a newline lets a caller forge log records). Commas and '|' stay legal deliberately. Reading is never refused, so events already stored under a rejected ID stay reachable."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_assertvalidpersistenceid", "label": "assertValidPersistenceId", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### What a persistence ID may contain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Exported so the same rules can be checked without starting an actor; the rules also run again inside journal.append() as defence in depth."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery", "label": "Recovery", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Recovery", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "preStart loads the latest snapshot, reads events from seqNr+1, folds each through onEvent, then fires onRecoveryComplete. No commands are processed while it runs; the mailbox piles up and is drained in order afterwards."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoverycomplete", "label": "onRecoveryComplete(state)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Recovery", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "One-time post-recovery setup hook. A throw from it is an ordinary actor failure that goes to supervision, not a recovery failure, because the state recovered fine."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "label": "onRecoveryFailure(reason)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### When recovery fails", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A notification, not a decision: recovery failure is terminal either way and the hook only chooses who hears about it. The actor cannot carry on because state was never assigned and lastSequenceNr is unknown, so stopping keeps that visible - queued commands become dead letters instead of vanishing into the stash."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "label": "JournalIntegrityError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### When recovery fails", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carries persistenceId and the offending sequenceNr so an operator sees which store broke its contract."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotintegrityerror", "label": "SnapshotIntegrityError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### When recovery fails", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The snapshot-side counterpart, carrying the same persistenceId and sequenceNr."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalcontractcheck", "label": "Replay's journal-contract check", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### What replay refuses to fold", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Before any event reaches onEvent, replay asserts sequence numbers are ascending, contiguous and inside the requested window. Fatal rather than a warning because the fold IS recovery: a shuffled stream replays history in an order it never happened in and leaves the sequence on the last event delivered, after which every persist fails with a JournalConcurrencyError pointing at a healthy journal. It also refuses a history whose beginning is missing - hence compact only past a snapshot."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotpolicy", "label": "snapshotPolicy()", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Snapshots", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Declares when to snapshot; everyNEvents(N) is the common case, a custom predicate covers event-kind or state-driven policies."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_everynevents", "label": "everyNEvents(N)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Snapshots", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_tagsfor", "label": "tagsFor(event)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Tagging events for projections", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asked once per event, including inside a persistAll, so a batch that mixes event kinds is tagged per kind and a projection filtering on one sees exactly its own events - while the batch is still written atomically."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_eventadapter", "label": "EventAdapter", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Schema evolution - event adapters", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Upgrades old events on read; with an adapter configured every event is wrapped in a { _v, _t, _e } envelope at persist time and unwrapped through fromJournal at read time. Backward compatibility stays the actor's responsibility."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_taggedjsontree", "label": "Tagged JSON tree payload format", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## What events and state may contain", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Every store on every backend writes payloads in the same tagged tree JsonSerializer uses, so Date/Map/Set/bigint/typed arrays round-trip as real instances without configuration and the in-memory stores behave like production. Errors round-trip deliberately WITHOUT the stack, because a persisted stack would leak filesystem paths into long-lived rows. Functions, symbols and cycles throw at persist time rather than corrupting the row."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_customserializerperstore", "label": "withSerializer(serializer) per store", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### Custom serializer per store", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The way to preserve class identity or use a binary row format; CborSerializer carries the whole round-trip table, a schema-driven serializer only knows its schema's fields."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_twowriters", "label": "Two writers for one entity", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Two writers for one entity", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A partition plus a rebalance, or an orchestration mistake, and two instances both recover and both accept commands. The journal survives it because appends are conditional on the sequence number; the damage is outside the journal, in side effects the loser already ran."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalconcurrencyerror", "label": "JournalConcurrencyError", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "## Two writers for one entity", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_lostracebackstop", "label": "Lost-race backstop: the actor stops", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### The backstop: a lost race stops the actor", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A JournalConcurrencyError is treated as evidence the instance lost an ownership race, so the actor stops rather than restarts - the default supervision answer is a restart, and a restarted loser would recover the now-foreign journal head and carry on serving as though it owned the entity. Costs nothing, needs no configuration, and cannot undo the side effect that already ran."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_lease", "label": "lease() fence on a PersistentActor", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### The fence: a lease", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Acquired in preStart BEFORE recovery, so an instance that does not own the entity never even reads its history and cannot serve stale answers. A non-holder's persist throws immediately instead of discovering the conflict at the journal, which keeps the duplicate side effect from firing at all."}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onleaselost", "label": "onLeaseLost(reason)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": "### The fence: a lease", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Defaults to stopping, because a PersistentActor that may not write is rarely usefully alive; override it to keep serving reads."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_oncommand", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_initialstate", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_oncommand", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persist", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persist", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onevent", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceid", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceid", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceidvalidation", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistenceidvalidation", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_assertvalidpersistenceid", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoverycomplete", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_onrecoveryfailure", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotintegrityerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_recovery", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalcontractcheck", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalcontractcheck", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_journalintegrityerror", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotpolicy", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_snapshotpolicy", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_everynevents", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_tagsfor", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_eventadapter", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_taggedjsontree", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_taggedjsontree", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_customserializerperstore", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/persistence/persistent-actor.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_persistence_persistent_actor_persistentactor", "target"